{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AB56YysKkaKfV8mvudrUNM","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0519-4/projects/policy_ambiguity_safety/ROADMAP.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# policy_ambiguity_safety — Research Dashboard\\\\n\\\\n> 最后更新: 2026-05-20 11:29 UTC | 更新原因: Research 阶段启动：MVP+diagnostic 完成，framing+plan 已创建，Dream 运行中\\\\n\\\\n## 核心方向\\\\n**Binary anchor**：歧义策略导致大规模 agent 安全违规（+31-42pp），且与歧义类型无关（uniform effect）。CL 贡献：nocuous ambiguity 理论 + visibility insight（显式冲突 < 隐形结构歧义）。详见 paper_framing.md。\\\\n\\\\n## 当前进展\\\\n- **阶段**: Research（MVP 完成，2 个实验收敛）\\\\n- **目标会议**: EMNLP 2026（ARR Aug cycle, DDL ~Aug 3, ~10 周）\\\\n- **mvp_001**: Type effect FAIL (p=0.50, V=0.084), binary effect +35-42pp (p<1e-6)\\\\n- **diag_001**: Layer effect FAIL (CP 34% vs scopal 40%, p=0.46). Visibility insight 发现。\\\\n- **paper_framing.md**: ✅ 已创建（C1-C5, 5 claims）\\\\n- **experiment_plan.yaml**: ✅ 已创建（8 experiments, P0-P2）\\\\n- **dream_simulate**: 🔄 dream_20260520T112859 运行中（full mode）\\\\n- **literature_map.yaml**: ✅ 已创建（13 篇核心论文）\\\\n\\\\n## 近期任务\\\\n- [ ] 等 Dream 回调 → 评估 framing/plan 是否需要调整\\\\n- [ ] plan_001: 生成 140 条新条款（coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20, incompleteness +20）\\\\n- [ ] plan_002: Full study API 端（1,200 episodes, gpt-5.4 + gpt-4.1）\\\\n- [ ] plan_003: Full study 本地端（1,200 episodes, Qwen3-8B + Qwen3-32B-AWQ, 需 GPU）\\\\n- [ ] 向用户确认 GPU 开机 + Anthropic API key\\\\n\\\\n## GPU 预算\\\\n- P0: 48h RTX PRO 6000（plan_003 本地推理）\\\\n- P1: 12h（plan_006 reliability replicates）\\\\n- P2: 8h（plan_008 classifier PoC）\\\\n- 总计: 68h | 当前分配: 0 GPU | 需用户开机\\\\n\\\\n## 时间线\\\\n| 周次 | 内容 |\\\\n|------|------|\\\\n| W1 (now) | Dream + plan_001 条款生成 + plan_007 realism validation |\\\\n| W2-3 | plan_002 API 实验 + plan_003 本地实验（需 GPU） |\\\\n| W3-4 | plan_004 统计分析 + plan_005 error analysis |\\\\n| W4 | plan_006 reliability test |\\\\n| W5-7 | Paper Agent 写作 |\\\\n| W8-9 | Reviewer iteration + 投稿准备 |\\\\n| W10 | ARR Aug 提交 |\\\\n\\\\n## 关键决策日志\\\\n\\\\n| ID | 日期 | 摘要 | 关联实验 |\\\\n|----|------|------|----------|\\\\n| D013 | 2026-05-20 | diag_001 FAIL: layer effect 不存在，C3 死亡。Paper framin | diag_001, mvp_001 |\\\\n| D012 | 2026-05-20 | Full study 新增 model×type interaction 作为正式分析维度 | mvp_001 |\\\\n| D011 | 2026-05-20 | MVP FAIL on type effect → pivot to binary anchor + | mvp_001 |\\\\n| D010 | 2026-05-20 | MVP 改用 gpt-5.4 + gpt-4.1（端点无 Claude），立即启动 | — |\\\\n| D009 | 2026-05-20 | API 阻塞解除：ECONNREFUSED 是 WebFetch 代理问题，端点从本机可达，MVP  | — |\\\\n| D008 | 2026-05-20 | Taxonomy 采用 2-layer 结构（3 linguistic + 3 specificat | — |\\\\n| D007 | 2026-05-20 | EMNLP 适配：保 6 类型、砍模型 6→4、砍条款 500→300、Phase 3 降级 PoC | — |\\\\n| D006 | 2026-05-20 | 目标会议从 ICLR 2027 切换至 EMNLP 2026（ARR Aug cycle） | — |\\\\n| D005 | 2026-05-20 | MVP 使用 τ²-bench + 剥离 tool description 中的策略信息 | — |\\\\n| D004 | 2026-05-20 | MVP 分析改为双轨：ambiguous-only 跨类型比较（主）+ matched-pair w | — |\\\\n\\\\n\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 2467, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WjqTeLLLBSPS4fQbQ6HiJR","session_id":"ed42e909-7586-4fce-8151-53367c735e4f","uuid":"d8e75ff1-927c-4792-ae6c-b267f14b34d9","timestamp":"2026-05-20T12:06:21.386Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VqGYqx3RjQpf4YbSXjM96F","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qf55rMjvpgPqRe6sUrrZ1V","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus is **novelty, positioning, and related work**. You are doing a blind review — evaluate the paper purely on its merits.\n\n## Venue Calibration (EMNLP 2026 via ARR)\n- 5 = Award (top 2.5%), 4 = Main conference, 3 = Findings, 2 = Resubmit, 1 = Do not resubmit\n- Dimensions: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5)\n- Acceptance rate ~21% for Main\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"All Ambiguity Is Nocuous: A Causal Study of Policy Specification Ambiguity and Agent Safety Violations\"\n\nThe paper studies how linguistic ambiguity in natural-language policy specifications causes safety violations in LLM agents. Using a matched-pair design, 300 clause pairs across 6 ambiguity types, 4 models (GPT-5.4, GPT-4.1, Qwen3-32B-AWQ, Qwen3-8B), and 2,400 agentic episodes on τ²-bench, they establish 5 claims:\n- C1: Ambiguous clauses cause +33.6 pp increase in violation rate (all 6 types p < 3e-7)\n- C2: Ambiguity type does not differentially predict violation severity (χ²(5)=5.20, p=0.39, V=0.066) — binary detection suffices\n- C3: Visible conflicts (CP) yield fewer violations than invisible ambiguity (scopal): Δ=-11pp, p=0.015\n- C4: Model capability predicts type sensitivity — stronger models show wider type-specific ranges (22pp vs 4pp), interaction p=0.018\n- C5: Error analysis identifies 8 failure modes with strong type-clustering\n\nThe paper connects to Berry & Kamsties' nocuous/innocuous ambiguity theory, arguing all policy ambiguity is nocuous for LLM agents (unlike human RE where shared context renders most innocuous).\n\nRelated work covers: ambiguity in NLP/RE (Wasow et al. 2005, Kennedy 2007, Berry & Kamsties 2003, Li et al. 2024, Massey et al. 2014, Chantree et al. 2006), agent safety evaluation (τ²-bench, PolicyBank, PhantomPolicy, DRIP-R), policy specification quality (prompt engineering, constitutional AI).\n\nA 6-type taxonomy is provided with cross-walk to 3 prior frameworks (Table 8). A PoC DeBERTa-v3-large binary classifier achieves 88% accuracy / AUC 0.93.\n\nPaper is 8 pages main text + references + 4 appendices. Anonymous.\n\nReferences list: Berry & Kamsties 2003, Chantree et al. 2006, DRIP-R 2026 (anonymous concurrent), Kennedy 2007, Li et al. 2024 (anonymous), Massey et al. 2014, τ²-bench 2025 (anonymous), Wasow et al. 2005.\n\n## Your Task\nProvide a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Novelty Assessment**:\n   - What is genuinely new? What is incremental?\n   - How does this advance beyond DRIP-R (concurrent, measures decision quality not safety violations)?\n   - Is the \"all ambiguity is nocuous\" theoretical framing novel and well-supported?\n   - Is extending Berry & Kamsties to LLM agents a meaningful contribution?\n3. **Related Work Gaps**:\n   - Missing citations or positioning gaps\n   - Are there obvious related works not discussed? (agent safety, ambiguity detection, specification quality, constitutional AI, prompt robustness, etc.)\n   - Is the differentiation from DRIP-R sufficient?\n4. **Strengths** (bulleted, specific)\n5. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, specific, with severity: major/minor)\n6. **Framing and Narrative Critique**:\n   - Is the title claim (\"All Ambiguity Is Nocuous\") well-supported by the evidence?\n   - Is C2 (type uniformity null) being over-interpreted? (absence of evidence vs. evidence of absence)\n   - Does the paper overclaim or underclaim?\n   - Is the visibility finding (C3) properly situated in psycholinguistic literature?\n7. **Questions for Authors** (3-5 specific questions)\n8. **Scores**:\n   - Soundness (1-5)\n   - Excitement (1-5)  \n   - Reproducibility (1-5)\n   - Overall Assessment (1-5, half-point scale per EMNLP 2026)\n   - Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Calibrate to EMNLP acceptance rate (~21% main, plus Findings). A paper scoring 4.0 is borderline Main acceptance."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":35650,"cache_read_input_tokens":23505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":35650},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ed42e909-7586-4fce-8151-53367c735e4f","uuid":"afb2c4ce-911b-458d-803d-41e79b06d7e7"}
{"type":"system","subtype":"task_started","task_id":"a953eb149446a6f88","tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qf55rMjvpgPqRe6sUrrZ1V","description":"R2: Novelty + Related Work review","task_type":"local_agent","prompt":"You are Reviewer R2 for an EMNLP 2026 submission. Your focus is **novelty, positioning, and related work**. You are doing a blind review — evaluate the paper purely on its merits.\n\n## Venue Calibration (EMNLP 2026 via ARR)\n- 5 = Award (top 2.5%), 4 = Main conference, 3 = Findings, 2 = Resubmit, 1 = Do not resubmit\n- Dimensions: Soundness (1-5), Excitement (1-5), Reproducibility (1-5)\n- Acceptance rate ~21% for Main\n\n## Paper Summary\nTitle: \"All Ambiguity Is Nocuous: A Causal Study of Policy Specification Ambiguity and Agent Safety Violations\"\n\nThe paper studies how linguistic ambiguity in natural-language policy specifications causes safety violations in LLM agents. Using a matched-pair design, 300 clause pairs across 6 ambiguity types, 4 models (GPT-5.4, GPT-4.1, Qwen3-32B-AWQ, Qwen3-8B), and 2,400 agentic episodes on τ²-bench, they establish 5 claims:\n- C1: Ambiguous clauses cause +33.6 pp increase in violation rate (all 6 types p < 3e-7)\n- C2: Ambiguity type does not differentially predict violation severity (χ²(5)=5.20, p=0.39, V=0.066) — binary detection suffices\n- C3: Visible conflicts (CP) yield fewer violations than invisible ambiguity (scopal): Δ=-11pp, p=0.015\n- C4: Model capability predicts type sensitivity — stronger models show wider type-specific ranges (22pp vs 4pp), interaction p=0.018\n- C5: Error analysis identifies 8 failure modes with strong type-clustering\n\nThe paper connects to Berry & Kamsties' nocuous/innocuous ambiguity theory, arguing all policy ambiguity is nocuous for LLM agents (unlike human RE where shared context renders most innocuous).\n\nRelated work covers: ambiguity in NLP/RE (Wasow et al. 2005, Kennedy 2007, Berry & Kamsties 2003, Li et al. 2024, Massey et al. 2014, Chantree et al. 2006), agent safety evaluation (τ²-bench, PolicyBank, PhantomPolicy, DRIP-R), policy specification quality (prompt engineering, constitutional AI).\n\nA 6-type taxonomy is provided with cross-walk to 3 prior frameworks (Table 8). A PoC DeBERTa-v3-large binary classifier achieves 88% accuracy / AUC 0.93.\n\nPaper is 8 pages main text + references + 4 appendices. Anonymous.\n\nReferences list: Berry & Kamsties 2003, Chantree et al. 2006, DRIP-R 2026 (anonymous concurrent), Kennedy 2007, Li et al. 2024 (anonymous), Massey et al. 2014, τ²-bench 2025 (anonymous), Wasow et al. 2005.\n\n## Your Task\nProvide a detailed review covering:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Novelty Assessment**:\n   - What is genuinely new? What is incremental?\n   - How does this advance beyond DRIP-R (concurrent, measures decision quality not safety violations)?\n   - Is the \"all ambiguity is nocuous\" theoretical framing novel and well-supported?\n   - Is extending Berry & Kamsties to LLM agents a meaningful contribution?\n3. **Related Work Gaps**:\n   - Missing citations or positioning gaps\n   - Are there obvious related works not discussed? (agent safety, ambiguity detection, specification quality, constitutional AI, prompt robustness, etc.)\n   - Is the differentiation from DRIP-R sufficient?\n4. **Strengths** (bulleted, specific)\n5. **Weaknesses** (bulleted, specific, with severity: major/minor)\n6. **Framing and Narrative Critique**:\n   - Is the title claim (\"All Ambiguity Is Nocuous\") well-supported by the evidence?\n   - Is C2 (type uniformity null) being over-interpreted? (absence of evidence vs. evidence of absence)\n   - Does the paper overclaim or underclaim?\n   - Is the visibility finding (C3) properly situated in psycholinguistic literature?\n7. **Questions for Authors** (3-5 specific questions)\n8. **Scores**:\n   - Soundness (1-5)\n   - Excitement (1-5)  \n   - Reproducibility (1-5)\n   - Overall Assessment (1-5, half-point scale per EMNLP 2026)\n   - Confidence (1-5)\n\nBe rigorous. Calibrate to EMNLP acceptance rate (~21% main, plus Findings). A paper scoring 4.0 is borderline Main acceptance.","uuid":"ac400f97-07a6-4fc9-b525-55b16d942d1c","session_id":"ed42e909-7586-4fce-8151-53367c735e4f"}
